YAAP -- Link the Male Gnome Neutral Healer

This ascension took longer than the others, because I started off with
a protection racket experiment, which involved me repeatedly trying
the protection racket (and #quitting afterward), to see if it can be a
reliable strategy.  I decided that the Gnome Healer is the only race/
class combination that should try the protection racket, and they
should try for 9 points of protection if possible.  And yes, it has to
be a Gnomish healer, as I think Human healers would be a terrible
choice for the protection racket, due to potential dark levels that
might occur in the Gnomish Mines above the Minetown.

The difficulty of the protection racket varied between games.  In one
game, I didn't have 5Pw, and the newts weren't giving me extra Pw, so
I had to go slower than normal, as the only way I could heal the pet
is with the limited number of healing potions that were in my starting
inventory.  In another game, there wasn't a General store, and the
other stores didn't have any expensive items -- so I went to one of
the shops, dumped all their items into a container, and had a pet
steal the container.  This allowed me to get extra gold from the
cheaper shops at a tolerable rate.  Fortunately, I had found a small
container in that game, as the worst case scenario would have been to
drag a chest all the way to the Minetown shop.  In a couple games, I
fell through a trap door, and had to write Elbereth in the dust way
too many times to get back to my pet.  It turns out the worst threat I
found was a gas spore, as they don't show up in infravision, and being
near one when your pet kills it can one-shot kill a level 1 Healer,
and that is taking into consideration the extra HP the Healers get for
quaffing some of their healing and extra healing potions.

After the protection racket, I did my normal "get a large stack of
poisoned darts" thing, which unfortunately caused me to lose a bunch
of potions when I randomly mixed them together in attemps to get a
potion of sickness.  Up until this point, I was using a runed dagger
to melee everything I can handle, with the pet dealing with the stuff
I couldn't melee.  A stack of daggers was too heavy at this point, so
I didn't bother to collect them.  The poisoned darts ended up being
used until I entered Gehennom, at which point I was level 30 with the
magic missile spell.

I found out that I like wis-based spellcasters, as even though I was
restricted in almost every spell school, I was still able to cast most
the spells in the game if I wore a robe.  For example, I used Magic
Mapping throughout Gehennom, and I was using cone of cold and fireball
on the Astral Plane.  Wis-based spellcasters are great because it's
easy to max wis.

The most annoying part of the game is that I somehow lost my gold
detection scrolls, and had to wield the amulet of yendor to get near a
portal, then zap a wand of secret door detection to find the portal.
The amulet didn't seem all very reliable?  Does it only potentially
give a message once every X turns?  It seemed like I sometimes would
pass through the same area a couple times before the amulet gave me a
message that the portal was near.



